-- ============================================================================
-- BACKEND-OWNED RULES (DOCUMENTATION ONLY - NOT DATABASE TRIGGERS)
-- ============================================================================
-- Laravel service/action layer MUST enforce at least these cross-table rules:
--
-- COMMUNITY
-- - Youth submits community application; verifier approves/revises/rejects.
-- - organizations.review_status tracks review lifecycle; operational_status tracks active/suspended/archive state.
-- - Only review_status='approved' + operational_status='active' organizations may publish operational content.
-- - Multiple managers are allowed; leader uniqueness is enforced by service logic.
--
-- ACTIVITY
-- - Activity must be reviewed by verifier before publication.
-- - If activity.program_id is set, activity.organization_id must match program.organization_id.
-- - Registration eligibility: dates, quota, age, identity verification, members_only.
-- - Every Activity must have >= 1 Activity Session before it can start; create one default session for simple events.
-- - Session times must fall within the Activity start_at/end_at window; enforce this in Laravel.
-- - Attendance is recorded per session using UNIQUE(activity_session_id, participation_id).
-- - Completion requires valid participation/attendance according to application rules. Attendance itself is evidence, not automatic completion.
-- - Activity Passport is composed from completed verified participations at query time.
--
-- PROGRAM
-- - Draft program may exist without activities.
-- - Proposal submission requires active organization and >= 1 linked activity.
-- - Program progress is calculated in Laravel; do not persist a mutable progress column.
-- - Final completion requires approved proposal, required logbook progress,
--   approved financial report, and approved final evaluation.
--
-- IDENTITY
-- - Admin owns personal-identity verification workflow.
-- - Verification documents remain private; never expose identity data in public portfolio.
--
-- PORTFOLIO
-- - Public by default at the portfolio level, with user-controlled section visibility.
-- - Sensitive identity/contact/address/document fields are always private by design.
--
-- AUDIT / NOTIFICATIONS
-- - Write audit_logs and notifications from the same Laravel DB transaction as
--   the state-changing command whenever atomicity is required.
--
-- TIMESTAMPS
-- - Laravel/Eloquent owns updated_at. There is deliberately no ON UPDATE clause.
-- - Laravel SoftDeletes owns deleted_at where the model uses soft deletion.
-- ============================================================================
